# Serena Navigation

## Purpose

Use Serena for non-trivial code navigation when the Serena server is configured, reachable, and its index covers the current checkout.

## Activation

Activate only for code tasks involving unfamiliar or shared behavior. Check that the current workspace and index are the intended ones and that freshness is acceptable before relying on results.

## Workflow

Start with precise symbol lookup, inspect definitions and callers/callees, then inspect relevant tests and contracts. Keep the repository as the source of truth.

## Non-applicability

Do not activate for non-code tasks, familiar code where targeted inspection is sufficient, or repositories without a configured Serena service.

## Fallback

If Serena is unavailable, stale, or incomplete, use the repository’s other configured navigation tools or targeted `rg` search. Do not claim symbol inspection occurred when it did not. Serena is advisory unless a separate enforced control says otherwise.

## Control status

This is advisory guidance; it does not enforce navigation or index freshness.
